        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): stabilize shared-profile queueing",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- serialize shared manual-login profile runs by default and persist FIFO waiters so newer callers cannot starve older ones\n- keep the browser lease through cleanup and keep shared Chrome alive when a queued caller is waiting for handoff\n- separate queue wait time from active browser/input time with an independently configurable queue timeout\n- retry prompt submission once only when DOM evidence proves the prompt is still in the composer and no turn was accepted\n- preserve target/runtime metadata when prompt commit verification fails, and persist terminal model state before terminal session metadata\n- update CLI, MCP, session, configuration, documentation, and regression coverage\n\n## Reproduction\n\nA neutral four-client browser stress run against one shared profile showed a newer poller acquiring the released slot ahead of an older waiter. Two later clients also reached terminal prompt-commit timeouts after a long preceding run, while raw session metadata retained a running model state.\n\nThe regression fixture now holds one active client, registers three independent waiters, releases each lease in turn, and asserts the persisted acquisition order. Separate coverage exercises queue timeout cleanup, shared-Chrome handoff, safe prompt resubmission, runtime preservation, and terminal metadata ordering.\n\n## Validation\n\n- focused browser acceptance suite: 39 passed\n- provider/performance regression suite after scope split: 23 passed\n- `pnpm test` (1582 passed, 43 skipped)\n- `pnpm run check`\n- `pnpm run build`\n- `git diff --check`\n- neutral four-client CLI live stress: all four sessions completed with verified Pro selection, expected markers, one shared Chrome PID/port, FIFO handoff, and an empty lease/waiter registry\n- neutral MCP dry-run and live smoke completed; live session returned the expected structured marker with verified Pro selection\n\n## Inspectable live proof\n\nThe redacted, public-safe proof artifact is tracked at\n[`docs/testing/pr-325-browser-queue-proof.md`](https://github.com/steipete/oracle/blob/9d15d2e67ea168fd6b1c7ad270645785c3b1b222/docs/testing/pr-325-browser-queue-proof.md).\nIt includes the four-client FIFO acquisition sequence, stable shared Chrome\nPID/port, terminal session and model states, transcript sizes, independent\nfive-second queue timeout behavior, canonical MCP parity, version-1 registry\nupgrade coverage, and the empty final lease/waiter registry.\n",
